      ⍝ Integer overflow → float promotion (IntCell::bif_multiply_ii()).
      ⍝ Unlike + and -, × promotes as soon as the product's magnitude
      ⍝ exceeds the conservative LARGE_INT/SMALL_INT threshold (≈9.2E18,
      ⍝ ⎕SYL "largest/smallest integer"), well before the exact int64
      ⍝ boundary (≈9.223E18) that + and - use. ⎕PP←17 so the promoted
      ⍝ (float) results print with enough digits to be unambiguous.
      ⍝
      ⎕PP←17

      ⍝ boundary: product is (just) below the conservative threshold,
      ⍝ stays integer even though it is far from the true int64 limit
      1000000000×9199999999
9199999999000000000
      26⎕CR 1000000000×9199999999
16

